Vivienne did the boring stuff,
What's she gonna do now?


01:15:24.486 --> 01:15:27.421
You offering?


01:15:27.489 --> 01:15:29.821
Wouldn't get past the door,


01:15:39.968 --> 01:15:43.802
- I'm beginning to like this,
- What's that?


01:15:43.872 --> 01:15:46.432
Being with you,


01:15:46.508 --> 01:15:48.567
Being with Linda,


01:15:50.545 --> 01:15:53.708
Being with myself, Again,


01:15:55.751 --> 01:16:00.484
Hey, and I'm having sex and these muffins
are great, That sort of thing,


01:16:00.555 --> 01:16:02.955
You be careful, Mr, Shifty,


01:16:36.925 --> 01:16:38.290
(doorbell)


01:16:38.360 --> 01:16:42.091
Sorry to call so early,
it's just, we had a collection,


01:16:42.164 --> 01:16:47.727
We got a wreath for the church, but I also
wanted to bring something else I had done,


01:16:47.803 --> 01:16:50.237
Oh, that's very kind,


01:16:50.305 --> 01:16:52.466
- Is she in?
- Oh, yes,


01:16:52.541 --> 01:16:54.566
Linda,


01:16:54.643 --> 01:16:56.975
Linda!


01:16:59.247 --> 01:17:01.442
I like your robe,


01:17:03.752 --> 01:17:06.016
Diane's brought you something,


01:17:13.562 --> 01:17:16.963
- What is it?
- It's a bereavement cookie,


01:17:17.032 --> 01:17:19.432
- I can't eat that,
- Oh?


01:17:19.501 --> 01:17:21.594
She's gluten free,


01:17:21.670 --> 01:17:23.661
Oh!


01:17:23.739 --> 01:17:25.900
Right,


01:17:25.974 --> 01:17:29.410
Well, waste not, want not,
I'll take it back,


01:17:29.478 --> 01:17:33.574
It's my nephew's
fifth birthday tomorrow so,,,


01:17:33.648 --> 01:17:35.912
I'll scrape the icing off,


01:17:35.984 --> 01:17:38.612
put some new numbers on,


01:17:38.687 --> 01:17:41.713
- A nice new number five,
- I'll scrape it,


01:17:46.895 --> 01:17:48.920
(Marilyn barking)


01:17:58.106 --> 01:18:00.267
There,


01:18:07.149 --> 01:18:09.014
Well,


01:18:09.084 --> 01:18:11.985
I'll see you both in church later,


01:18:12.621 --> 01:18:14.452
(Alex) Um,,,


01:18:27.803 --> 01:18:31.261
- Thanks, Diane,
- Bye,


01:18:48.623 --> 01:18:53.822
Despite both our faults, I actually think
we work quite well together, don't you?


01:18:53.895 --> 01:18:57.763
Yes, I do,
Can you please take the dog out now?


01:18:57.833 --> 01:19:00.393
I don't want to talk to you anymore,


01:19:04.339 --> 01:19:10.300
- Shall I come back in about half an hour?
- I don't know, I only know how I feel now,


01:19:20.922 --> 01:19:22.913
(woman sobs)


01:19:25.894 --> 01:19:28.089
(muffled speech)


01:19:35.437 --> 01:19:38.167
Hello,
You must be Alex,


01:19:38.240 --> 01:19:40.231
I'm Dirk,


01:19:42.844 --> 01:19:45.506
And this is Ellen,


01:19:46.481 --> 01:19:48.540
How do you do?


01:19:48.617 --> 01:19:51.882
I'm sorry,
I told myself I wasn't gonna cry,


01:19:51.953 --> 01:19:56.856
Every time we go away, it's always Linda
we're worried about, isn't it, Dirk?


01:19:56.925 --> 01:20:01.862
We never even gave Vivienne
a second thought, We ne,,, we never,,,


01:20:03.431 --> 01:20:05.558
Ellen's a bit upset,


01:20:05.634 --> 01:20:10.037
We've been hiking,
We came straight here, Is Linda inside?


01:20:10.105 --> 01:20:12.266
I'm half inside, half outside,


01:20:21.082 --> 01:20:23.312
Hi, sweetie,


01:20:23.385 --> 01:20:25.216
Hi,


01:20:25.287 --> 01:20:28.222
We've just been meeting Alex, Linda,


01:20:30.558 --> 01:20:32.753
Your eyes are red,


01:20:32.827 --> 01:20:35.295
Yes, they are,


01:20:39.367 --> 01:20:44.327
- Mommy, cheek,
- Yeah, That's my girl, That's my,,,


01:20:46.574 --> 01:20:49.668
- I'll let you have some time,
- Yes,


01:20:49.744 --> 01:20:51.803
Thank you, Alex,


01:21:33.922 --> 01:21:39.019
I thought Vivienne would appreciate
something a bit unconventional,


01:21:39.094 --> 01:21:41.688
Perfectamundo,


01:21:43.331 --> 01:21:46.266
Is it compulsory to cry at funerals?


01:21:48.503 --> 01:21:51.631
No, It's not compulsory,


01:21:51.706 --> 01:21:55.039
Good, because I don't know
if I will or not,


01:22:01.249 --> 01:22:04.844
Wilson Bentley,
the man who photographed snowflakes,


01:22:04.919 --> 01:22:08.047
died after walking in a snowstorm,


01:22:13.962 --> 01:22:16.453
Is there anything you need?


01:22:19.701 --> 01:22:21.532
Yes,


01:22:28.877 --> 01:22:33.746
I'd like you to put your arms around me
and squeeze me really hard,


01:22:33.815 --> 01:22:36.784
but don't touch me
with your hands,


01:22:54.736 --> 01:22:57.102
Say when,


01:22:57.172 --> 01:23:00.073
(Linda sighs)


01:23:08.716 --> 01:23:12.413
(organ plays "Just Looking"
by Stereophonics)


01:23:53.461 --> 01:23:55.952
(Ellen) Linda, Linda,


01:23:56.030 --> 01:23:58.760
- Please sit down,
- Linda,


01:24:07.408 --> 01:24:09.239
(door shuts)


01:24:11.646 --> 01:24:13.045
(music stops)


01:24:54.022 --> 01:24:56.547
For those who don't know,


01:24:57.559 --> 01:24:59.891
I'm Vivienne's granddad,


01:25:00.929 --> 01:25:04.160
But as our daughter Linda
was unable to look after her,


01:25:04.232 --> 01:25:09.397
my wife Ellen and I
raised Vivienne as our own for 16 years,


01:25:13.208 --> 01:25:16.143
Vivienne was a real one-off,


01:25:16.211 --> 01:25:21.979
and the most gentle
and generous person I've ever met,


01:25:22.050 --> 01:25:24.143
She had an amazing ability -


01:25:24.219 --> 01:25:28.519
accepting people for what they are,
embracing their differences,


01:25:29.591 --> 01:25:32.526
Most of you
are probably aware that, um,,,


01:25:34.662 --> 01:25:36.960
Vivienne wanted to be a writer,


01:25:37.966 --> 01:25:41.265
On her last visit to us
only a week or so ago,


01:25:42.270 --> 01:25:47.537
she gave me a children's picture book
that she was working on,


01:25:48.810 --> 01:25:51.210
I'd like to read it to you


01:25:51.279 --> 01:25:56.376
because it says more about Vivienne
than anything I could put into words,


01:26:01.556 --> 01:26:03.888
"My Little Brother,"


01:26:03.958 --> 01:26:06.426
"My little brother James is special,


01:26:07.428 --> 01:26:11.626
"My little brother is four
and he can't talk yet,


01:26:12.500 --> 01:26:14.991
"He doesn't always understand
what I say to him,


01:26:15.069 --> 01:26:18.436
"and he's not a bit interested
in my wrestling toys,


01:26:18.506 --> 01:26:24.001
"Dad plays games with him and tries to
get him interested in rockets and football,


01:26:24.078 --> 01:26:27.980
"but my little brother
really only likes the alphabet,


01:26:28.049 --> 01:26:31.883
"He's very happy when we have
alphabet spaghetti for lunch,


01:26:31.953 --> 01:26:34.114
"but then, so am I,


01:26:42.397 --> 01:26:46.299
"Yesterday, he took my hands
and danced with me,


01:26:46.367 --> 01:26:50.929
"Every time he does something new,
however small,


01:26:52.774 --> 01:26:55.470
"it's a brilliant feeling,


01:26:55.543 --> 01:26:59.479
"I wish everyone could get to know
someone like my little brother,


01:26:59.547 --> 01:27:03.313
"He makes you look at things
in a brand-new way,


01:27:04.986 --> 01:27:10.686
"Some people say that James won't ever
do the things I do, but it doesn't matter,


01:27:10.758 --> 01:27:13.158
"He'll just do different things,


01:27:15.563 --> 01:27:21.968
"I love my little brother so much and, one
day, I know he'll tell me he loves me too,


01:27:23.504 --> 01:27:28.806
"Although he'll probably
spell it out in spaghetti first,"


01:27:34.882 --> 01:27:37.578
Thank you, Dirk,


01:27:37.652 --> 01:27:41.986
Please stand while we take a moment to
listen to one of Vivienne's favorite records,


01:27:42.056 --> 01:27:44.820
by the, uh,,,
(clears throat)


01:27:44.892 --> 01:27:47.884
Super Furry Animals,


01:27:47.962 --> 01:27:50.863
([music] "Hello Sunshine"
by Super Furry Animals)


01:28:41.649 --> 01:28:43.640
(people chatter)


01:29:01.669 --> 01:29:03.159
(doorbell)


01:29:04.906 --> 01:29:07.875
Oh, hi,
Thank you so much,


01:29:07.942 --> 01:29:11.241
Please take your shoes off
before entering,


01:29:14.148 --> 01:29:16.139
Excuse me,


01:29:17.518 --> 01:29:19.782
Why is that man still here?


01:29:19.854 --> 01:29:24.655
- Go on, Linda, hand these around,
- All these people doing social,


01:29:24.725 --> 01:29:28.923
- It's OK, Linda,
- It's not OK, When are they gonna go?


01:29:28.996 --> 01:29:33.023
Well, they'll have a sandwich
and then they'll go,


01:29:43.544 --> 01:29:46.069
So what do you see in him, Maggie?


01:29:47.081 --> 01:29:51.484
You know, Clyde,
you have a superior air about you,


01:29:51.552 --> 01:29:54.043
Whoever told you
you were so special?


01:29:54.121 --> 01:29:56.521
Whoever told you
you weren't?


01:30:01.229 --> 01:30:05.063
- It's surprisingly clean, eh?
- That's autism, They're neat freaks,


01:30:05.132 --> 01:30:08.124
Yeah? You should take notes,
You could learn something,


01:30:08.202 --> 01:30:11.399
- Why do you have to do that?
- What? It was a joke,


01:30:11.472 --> 01:30:13.997
Try one of these,
They're gluten free,


01:30:18.913 --> 01:30:24.351
You know, Alex is very fond of you,
He talks about you all the time,


01:30:25.353 --> 01:30:28.413
Maybe when he's gone,
I could come over and,,,


01:30:28.489 --> 01:30:31.083
Why would I want you
to come over?


01:30:33.728 --> 01:30:36.697
They've had sandwiches,
Why are they hanging around?


01:30:37.732 --> 01:30:42.499
Oh, thank you so much for coming,
It's very nice of you,


01:30:50.411 --> 01:30:51.571
(gasps)


01:31:20.274 --> 01:31:22.799
It's a funny place, this,


01:31:22.877 --> 01:31:25.141
Never felt at home here,


01:31:27.648 --> 01:31:33.712
But Linda always liked it, We bought it
because she wanted to be independent,


01:31:33.788 --> 01:31:36.655
especially after Vivienne was born,


01:31:41.295 --> 01:31:44.093
How did that happen?


01:31:45.099 --> 01:31:46.760
Um,,,


01:31:47.935 --> 01:31:50.529
We still don't know,


01:31:50.605 --> 01:31:52.596
She was very close -


01:31:52.673 --> 01:31:57.133
well, relatively close -
to a boy who went to the center,


01:31:58.546 --> 01:32:01.310
We all assumed
it was an experiment,


01:32:01.382 --> 01:32:05.751
She didn't seem remotely upset at first,
but she might have been forced,


01:32:05.820 --> 01:32:08.345
We asked and we asked,


01:32:09.357 --> 01:32:14.852
Anyhow, she was six months gone
before anyone noticed,


01:32:18.032 --> 01:32:20.296
It's like everything with Linda,


01:32:21.335 --> 01:32:23.929
You have to accept her totally,


01:32:25.072 --> 01:32:29.805
And somehow, Vivienne understood that
from very early on,


01:32:30.811 --> 01:32:33.803
Oh, she would've loved the service,


01:32:33.881 --> 01:32:36.315
And this, too,
She loved a party,


01:32:37.351 --> 01:32:40.684
I don't think there's ever been
more than five people in this house,


01:32:40.755 --> 01:32:43.588
I don't know
how you persuaded her,


01:32:44.592 --> 01:32:47.152
But, anyway,
I just wanted to say thanks,


01:32:47.228 --> 01:32:49.788
For staying,
You didn't have to,


01:32:49.864 --> 01:32:53.766
To be honest, the elements were
against me, I didn't have an alternative,


01:32:53.834 --> 01:32:56.359
There's always an alternative, Alex,


01:32:58.939 --> 01:33:03.376
This house is getting
nasty, nasty, nasty!


01:33:05.212 --> 01:33:08.875
("Notteru Ondo" by The Drifters
plays very loudly)


01:33:08.949 --> 01:33:11.076
It's all right, honey,


01:33:28.703 --> 01:33:31.638
(Linda sings along to music)


01:33:39.080 --> 01:33:40.638
Linda,


01:33:40.715 --> 01:33:43.013
I think you should stop now,


01:33:43.084 --> 01:33:45.314
No, it's all right, just,,,


01:33:45.386 --> 01:33:48.048
- Can't somebody turn this off?
- Leave her alone,


01:33:48.122 --> 01:33:50.989
- Linda, come on,
- She's OK,


01:33:52.760 --> 01:33:53.818
(turns off music)


01:33:53.894 --> 01:33:55.987
- She's fine,
- But this is a wake,


01:33:56.063 --> 01:33:59.590
She's fine,
Just let her dance,


01:33:59.667 --> 01:34:02.727
- Please!
- (music starts again)


01:34:11.378 --> 01:34:14.279
(sings along to music)


01:36:20.307 --> 01:36:24.767
It's like getting back on your bike,
You'll be fine,


01:36:24.845 --> 01:36:28.303
There's no point worrying
it'll happen again, Nothing you can do,


01:36:28.382 --> 01:36:33.410
- If it's coming, it's coming,
- Thank you, Clyde, That's very reassuring,


01:36:34.722 --> 01:36:37.384
I can't say I'm sad to see you go,


01:36:41.328 --> 01:36:43.489
Don't tell me,


01:36:43.564 --> 01:36:45.088
Maggie,


01:36:45.165 --> 01:36:46.564
Yep,


01:36:47.735 --> 01:36:50.226
- Do you think she'll ever,,,
- No,


01:36:53.474 --> 01:36:55.533
Drive safely, then,


01:37:05.586 --> 01:37:10.250
- Hi,
- I'm never having that many people here,


01:37:10.324 --> 01:37:13.157
- Where are your parents?
- I told them to go,


01:37:13.227 --> 01:37:16.219
I had to clean the house,
They'll be back tomorrow,


01:37:16.297 --> 01:37:18.925
Oh, right,


01:37:18.999 --> 01:37:22.127
I would've liked
to have said goodbye,


01:37:22.202 --> 01:37:25.069
- I'm gonna take Marilyn for a walk,
- Don't forget the,,,


01:37:25.139 --> 01:37:28.506
Garbage,
I know, 12 o'clock,


01:37:31.879 --> 01:37:33.540
(Maggie) Hi,


01:37:33.614 --> 01:37:36.105
We've just come to say goodbye,


01:37:36.183 --> 01:37:38.777
"We"?


01:37:38.852 --> 01:37:42.948
Any chance you'd keep an eye on her?
She'll be dead in a week otherwise,


01:37:43.023 --> 01:37:45.116
Who? Linda or the dog?


01:37:48.462 --> 01:37:51.431
She didn't take long to settle in,


01:37:53.801 --> 01:37:55.996
Maybe I should do the same,


01:37:56.070 --> 01:38:01.804
I saw this house in the real-estate window
in town, It's by the lake,


01:38:01.875 --> 01:38:04.002
Kind of tempting,


01:38:10.017 --> 01:38:13.043
No, Stupid idea,


01:38:13.120 --> 01:38:15.850
I told you I was selfish,


01:38:16.790 --> 01:38:18.849
You did,


01:38:23.197 --> 01:38:26.394
I hope you find what you're looking for
in Winnipeg,


01:38:26.467 --> 01:38:27.866
Mm,


01:38:27.935 --> 01:38:30.904
I wonder what that is,
Good luck to me,


01:38:41.415 --> 01:38:43.849
Maggie, I killed a man,


01:38:45.919 --> 01:38:48.649
The driver who ran into my son,


01:38:51.859 --> 01:38:54.794
I found out his name,
where he lived,


01:38:56.463 --> 01:38:58.590
I went there and I hit him,


01:39:01.035 --> 01:39:03.469
Hard,


01:39:03.537 --> 01:39:05.528
He fell,


01:39:06.607 --> 01:39:09.701
He fell onto this stone floor


01:39:12.479 --> 01:39:15.209
and he cracked his head open,


01:39:16.216 --> 01:39:18.275
I know,


01:39:18.352 --> 01:39:20.445
Clyde told me,


01:39:23.290 --> 01:39:27.386
- Why didn't you,,,
- I was waiting for you to mention it,


01:39:27.461 --> 01:39:30.191
I'm glad you did,


01:39:30.264 --> 01:39:33.961
You know,
mostly he's upset that you hit a cop,


01:39:36.003 --> 01:39:37.994
Thanks,


01:39:39.106 --> 01:39:43.065
I think you're gonna find peace
when you get there,


01:39:44.344 --> 01:39:46.574
You'll probably end up staying,


01:39:47.681 --> 01:39:51.640
But if you're ever
passing through here again, I,,,


01:39:51.718 --> 01:39:53.948
I've had a really nice time,


01:39:55.556 --> 01:39:57.786
Gotta do the garbage,
Gotta do the garbage, Garbage,


01:39:57.858 --> 01:40:01.419
Gotta do the garbage, Gotta do
the garbage, Gotta do the garbage,


01:40:01.495 --> 01:40:04.487
They're two hours late,
Maybe they're not coming today,


01:40:04.565 --> 01:40:08.262
What if we do what everybody in
the street - everybody in the world - does?


01:40:08.335 --> 01:40:12.669
Put the bags out, then if they don't turn up
today, you can leave them out until they do,


01:40:12.739 --> 01:40:17.233
No, we're not gonna do that, The bags
will split and that's when raccoons come,


01:40:17.311 --> 01:40:20.371
Raccoons have rabies
and they mess up the snow,


01:40:20.447 --> 01:40:23.211
I'm sorry, Linda,
I just don't know what else I can do,


01:40:23.283 --> 01:40:26.081
- I've made arrangements,
- You are a very selfish man,


01:40:26.153 --> 01:40:29.316
- No, I'm not, You're just unreasonable,
- I'm autistic,


01:40:29.389 --> 01:40:32.187
Well, it's the same thing,


01:40:32.259 --> 01:40:36.889
Apart from today, you have been very
helpful, Alex, and I want to say thank you,


01:40:36.964 --> 01:40:41.663
You're not as interesting as Vivienne, but
you have some quite good characteristics,


01:40:41.735 --> 01:40:43.600
Whoo-hoo,


01:40:43.670 --> 01:40:47.606
Don't go overboard
with the praise there, Linda,


01:40:56.984 --> 01:40:59.578
So, Linda,


01:41:01.421 --> 01:41:04.515
I'm really going to have to go,


01:41:06.426 --> 01:41:08.758
Very soon,


01:41:17.271 --> 01:41:19.899
You have been very annoying,


01:41:21.875 --> 01:41:25.641
But you've also been a friend
and I'm going to miss you,


01:41:31.251 --> 01:41:33.048
Hm,


01:41:34.221 --> 01:41:37.384
I didn't think
it'd be so hard to say goodbye,


01:41:39.593 --> 01:41:42.926
It's been a real pleasure,


01:41:44.831 --> 01:41:49.495
You are the only person
I have ever met


01:41:50.637 --> 01:41:56.041
who I didn't have to explain
or even justify myself to,


01:41:57.344 --> 01:41:59.869
Perfectamundo,


01:42:03.450 --> 01:42:06.510
- Sorry about the trash,
- Mm,


01:42:13.594 --> 01:42:17.052
- Can I send you a postcard?
- What for?


01:42:20.334 --> 01:42:23.735
- I'll give you a ring, I've got your number,
- When will you ring me?


01:42:23.804 --> 01:42:26.500
You know,
I think Vivienne would've liked our story,


01:42:26.573 --> 01:42:29.770
Well, she's not here to see it, is she?


01:42:33.146 --> 01:42:35.137
Right, then,


01:42:39.186 --> 01:42:42.451
I'm so sorry
about your daughter,


01:42:50.297 --> 01:42:52.993
I'm off,


01:42:56.436 --> 01:42:58.927
I left something for you,


01:43:00.107 --> 01:43:02.439
It's in the freezer,


01:43:19.626 --> 01:43:21.617
(car starts)


01:43:34.007 --> 01:43:35.941
(Linda sighs)


01:43:48.955 --> 01:43:51.116
Snow cake,


01:43:52.125 --> 01:43:54.616
Now, that is interesting,


01:44:22.556 --> 01:44:24.547
(dog barks outside)


01:44:25.926 --> 01:44:27.917
Oh, no!


01:44:31.231 --> 01:44:33.199
(door slams)


01:45:11.638 --> 01:45:14.038
(Linda) He stops for one second.


01:45:14.107 --> 01:45:17.565
And he's totally overwhelmed
by how big the world is


01:45:17.644 --> 01:45:20.545
and how small
and unimportant he is.


01:45:20.614 --> 01:45:22.673
And as he turns around,


01:45:22.749 --> 01:45:25.479
we see his face look to the sky.


01:45:25.552 --> 01:45:27.850
And he says, very quietly,


01:45:27.921 --> 01:45:30.651
